    {
      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <climits>\n#include <omp.h>\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\n    \n    // Use flat array for matrix (row-major)\n    std::vector<int> mat(n * n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            scanf(\"%d\", &mat[i * n + j]);\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Prefix sum matrix of size (n+1)x(n+1), using long long to avoid overflow\n    int stride = n + 1;\n    std::vector<long long> pref(stride * stride, 0);\n\n    // First pass: row-wise prefix sums (parallel)\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        long long row_sum = 0;\n        int base_in = i * n;\n        int base_out = (i + 1) * stride;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            row_sum += mat[base_in + j];\n            pref[base_out + j + 1] = row_sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Second pass: column-wise prefix sums on the result (parallel)\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n        long long col_sum = 0;\n        int col_idx = j + 1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n            col_sum += pref[(i + 1) * stride + col_idx];\n            pref[(i + 1) * stride + col_idx] = col_sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Search all top-left corners of SxS submatrices (parallel with reduction)\n    long long mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\n    #pragma omp parallel for collapse(2) schedule(guided) reduction(max:mxSum)\n    for (int i = 0; i <= n - s; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j <= n - s; ++j) {\n            long long sum = pref[(i + s) * stride + j + s]\n                          - pref[i * stride + j + s]\n                          - pref[(i + s) * stride + j]\n                          + pref[i * stride + j];\n            if (sum > mxSum) mxSum = sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", mxSum);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Use integral image (prefix sum matrix) computed via two-pass parallel prefix sums with static scheduling, then search all top-left corners using collapse(2) guided schedule reduction(max). This demonstrates OpenMP work sharing through parallel for directives on both construction and search phases, reductions via max reduction, explicit scheduling control (static for regular workload of prefix sums, guided for adaptive load balancing in search), and thread granularity via collapsed loops.",
  "notes": "Use flat arrays to improve cache locality. Use long long for prefix sums to avoid overflow. The algorithm is changed from sliding window to integral image to enable parallelism.",
